ction, or just too many cars. All produce the same "jam" (cold), but fixing each cause requires different solutions. 4) Tie it back to why a cure is hard: because you'd need a different drug for each virus, and there are too many. So it's not that it's 200 different diseases, it's that the one disease (cold) has many different starting points. That's why it's hard to find a single cure. I'll keep it friendly and not condescending. Use conversational tone.
